WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.010
- This should be a weapon
in the Hunger Games arena.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:07.800
(electronic music)

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.690
- I like that it has an
eggplant emoji on the front.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:20.820
Or maybe I don't.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.190
- It looks almost the
same color as my nail.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.110
(makes disgusted sounds)

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.150
- I think you just gave me paint.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.030
I don't think this is a real toothpaste.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.450
- Alright I'm done, alright.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.193
This is it?

00:00:31.193 --> 00:00:32.750
- Taylor would you please smell my breath?

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.740
- Sure.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.240
- It seriously smells like nothing.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.840
- I'm actually getting minty smells.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:39.670
- How!?

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.880
(electronic music)

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.840
- I am terrified.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.750
- I'm not like as much of an enthusiast

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.350
as most of the people on the internet.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.420
But I like bacon, don't
get me wrong, I like bacon.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.384
- It is a breakfast food
though, so I guess it works

00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:51.380
in the morning.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.384
- It does smell a lot like bacon.

00:00:53.384 --> 00:00:56.180
- It smells like a dog who
just ate Beggin' Strips

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.480
and puked it up all over the floor.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.820
So I'm pretty excited to put
it in my mouth right now.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.110
(brushing sounds)

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:04.900
- Nope.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.700
- This is not messing around,
it actually tastes like bacon.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.740
- There aren't really
words to describe this.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.620
- I've already brushed twice,
I wanna keep brushing more

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.080
because it's enjoyable.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.210
- Give it to me, let's go.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.620
- Okay.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.573
- Oh!

00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:19.710
- Christmas sausage.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.590
- It's bacon.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.840
- Uh, that's gross.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.340
(electronic music)

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.970
- Oh my God, jasmine mint,
that sounds like a toothpaste

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.680
flavor, unlike eggplant or bacon.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.680
- Can we just take a moment
to appreciate this packaging?

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.640
- It makes me feel like this
is what they used in the

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.890
olden days.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.980
I don't think that's
accurate but, you know.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.897
- It's like...

00:01:40.897 --> 00:01:44.021
there's a flower on my toothbrush.

00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:45.070
(grunts)

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.360
- This is a toothpaste you
could take home to Mom.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.570
- This is the only one that
rivals normal toothpaste

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.530
in the way that it tastes.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.070
- When you're done with
this could I have this?

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.250
Because this is really great.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.790
- Um...

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.620
- Well first of all, your breath is bad.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.613
- That's actually enjoyable.

00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:02.380
- It totally smells like jasmine tea.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.623
- I'd make out with
somebody who used this.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.050
(electronic music)

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:09.050
- I'm kind of nervous about this.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.470
- It smells like curry, I
don't know why you would ever

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.720
wanna brush your teeth
to smell like curry.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.220
(brushing sounds)

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:17.230
- Help.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.770
- (laughing) It's really bad.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.270
- There's like a refreshing-ness

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.940
that's surprising to the curry.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.530
- Just the way he's
smacking his lips is scaring

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.850
the heck out of me.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.990
(exhales)

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.610
- That does not smell like curry.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.570
- That's gnarly.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.530
- That was a really strange
experiment that I just

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.620
participated in.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.192
- The best part about this
week was that I got to

00:02:36.192 --> 00:02:37.660
brush my teeth after lunch.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.330
I get you Brazilians.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.600
- It's hard to pick which
one is the absolute worst,

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.920
'cause they're all bad.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.460
- I don't care if Target
has a deal on any of these,

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.760
I'm never buying them, I'm
not buying two for one,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.420
or ten for seven, no.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.760
- Yeah, I'll stick to
the regular toothpaste.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.470
I like feeling so fresh and so clean.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.220
- Sure, why not?

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.310
- Are you gonna keep
asking us whether we'd

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.464
make our together?

00:02:58.464 --> 00:03:00.020
- Do you just want us to make out?

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.319
(piano note)

